message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: Calibrated Committee
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: Spark AI NLP
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/calibrated-committee
abstract: >-
  Learned aggregation for a heterogeneous committee of holographic
  membranes: per-member vote weights fit by multiclass logistic
  regression on calibration trials, frozen, evaluated on fresh
  seeds with structural calibrate/evaluate separation. A deepened
  negative result: the fit learns a dictatorship of the best
  member, a richer 20-parameter stacking does no better, and the
  oracle gap stands -- the oracle information is not in the votes
  in any linearly extractable form.
keywords:
  - holographic-memory
  - ensemble
  - stacking
  - calibration
  - negative-result
